WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.850
Your agents. Your repos. Your data. Your infrastructure.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.850
Otto: every coding agent, one native Mac app.

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.850
Home shows live sessions, dashboards, usage and findings.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.850
Light, dark and right-to-left, one design system.

5
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.850
Press ⌘K, type or speak. Otto runs it or answers.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.850
⌥Space calls the bar from anywhere on your Mac.

7
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.850
Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity and shells run as real sessions.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.850
Tile live terminals, or broadcast one prompt to many.

9
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:33.850
Threads run your agents on the structured runtime: plans, commands and diffs stream live.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.850
Approve inline, or ask another agent from inside the thread: its answer arrives as a live card.

11
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.850
Council sends one prompt to several agents, side by side.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.850
Synthesize: a judge compares the answers and picks or merges.

13
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.850
Give a goal and acceptance checks.

14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.850
Goal loops plan, execute and evaluate until every check passes.

15
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.850
Workflows chain agents, approvals and tools.

16
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.850
Scheduled tasks run agents on a cadence and report back.

17
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.850
A personal agent's Chat is a thread on the same runtime, with its tools.

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.850
Each agent runs its routines on a schedule and reports back.

19
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.850
A commit graph with your work in progress and pull requests.

20
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.850
Multi-agent code review turns findings into tracked fixes.

21
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.850
A story's Design tab lists the designs that implement it.

22
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.850
Design Hall is the one home for designs: compare versions, restore or approve one.

23
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.850
The Vault links your markdown docs with backlinks and live context.

24
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.850
Skills Lab is the one home for your agent skills.

25
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.850
Query MySQL, Postgres, MongoDB, Redis and ClickHouse.

26
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.850
A read-only connection refuses writes. History spans every connection.

27
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.850
SSH, AWS, Kubernetes, APIs and the web.

28
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.850
MCP servers run native or governed. A dangerous tool call waits for a person.

29
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.850
Insights turns your activity into key findings.

30
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.850
Usage shows what is left on each plan, per login.

31
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.850
Start a room from a live session. The host admits who joins.

32
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.850
Share a screen and talk it through.

33
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.850
Teammates draw on the shared screen, with permission.

34
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.850
Hand over terminal control, and take it back at any time.

35
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.850
With everyone's consent, get a local recap: decisions and action items.

36
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.850
Continue on phone: scan, approve the match on your Mac, and the thread opens.

37
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.850
Or switch the phone to the light version: five tabs, one tap back.

38
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:29.850
Snip the screen, bridge Slack and Telegram, and take Otto with you.

39
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.850
Otto. All your agents, one home.
